scope: branch
base: main@8f1c2ab
head: cursor/rate-limit-search@d4e91f0
repo: acme/storefront
tags:
  - api
  - reliability
summary: |
  One integration partner was issuing ~40 search requests a second, which
  saturated the read replica and slowed checkout for everyone. This adds a
  fixed-window limiter in front of `/api/search` only: 100 requests per
  minute per API key, `429` with `Retry-After` when exceeded.

  It deliberately does not touch the other routes. The window is stored in
  Redis with `INCR` + `EXPIRE`, so it is shared across the four app
  instances rather than per-process.
checks:
  - cmd: npm test -- rate-limit
    status: pass
    detail: 11 tests, including the boundary at exactly 100
    ran: 2026-09-14T09:10:44Z
